   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to making technical changes; and to\namend chapter 507 of the laws of 2016, relating to the imposition of an\noccupancy tax in the village of Harrison, in relation to extending the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5783",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5783-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Ren §1202-dd to be 1202-dd-1, Tax L; amd §2, Chap 507 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5783\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to making technical  changes;\nand to amend chapter 507 of the laws of 2016, relating to the imposition\nof an occupancy tax in the village of Harrison, in relation to extending\nthe effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend by two years the authorization for\nthe Village of Harrison to have a room occupancy tax not to exceed 3%.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 renumbers the relevant section of tax law.\n\nSection 2 extends from September 1, 2025 to September 1, 2027 the\nauthorization for the Village of Harrison to have a room occupancy tax.\n\nSection 3 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe village of Harrison seeks the continued authority to impose a 3%\ndaily room tax on any room in a hotel, motel, or similar place. This tax\nraises revenues to support municipal expenses while staying within the\nproperty tax cap. Initially granted by Chapter 507 of the Laws of 2016\nthis bill would again extend the expiration date of this authority.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: Ch. 423\n\n2019: Ch. 205\n\n2016: Ch. 507\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
